Human: Can you tell me the steps to write an if/then statement in C programming language?

Assistant: Sure, here’s how you could write an “if-then” statement in C:

if (condition)
{
  // code to execute if condition is true
}
else
{
  // code to execute if condition is false
}

You can extract the individual parts of this into variables if you like. This code will check if a number is positive or negative. If it’s positive, it will print “positive”, if it’s negative it will print “negative”.
